Clicks 1.0 for RISC OS
======================

An example desktop program from riscos-crossdev: a Wimp task written in C,
cross-compiled on Linux with GCCSDK GCC 10.2, tested there against the Fake
RISC OS, checked, and zipped with RISC OS filetypes.

Double-click !Clicks. Its icon appears on the icon bar.

  Select on the icon     opens the window
  Select in the window   counts a click
  Adjust in the window   starts the count again
  Menu on the icon       Quit

Requirements: RISC OS 5 on an ARMv7 machine with VFP (a Raspberry Pi 2
or later, or a Cortex-A8/A9 board); SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later and
ARMEABISupport, both from PackMan.

